85
00:22:22,195 --> 00:22:32,056
progress and manage that real-world problem or a workflow or any kind of process, etc.

86
00:22:32,056 --> 00:22:41,056
Therefore, every real-world entity in our problem domain will be mapped onto programming constructs.

87
00:22:41,971 --> 00:22:51,672
And every real-world entity in the problem domain will be treated as objects in our application, in our code.

88
00:22:52,432 --> 00:22:59,912
Therefore, an object in an object-oriented code will be corresponding to a real-world entity.

89
00:23:03,192 --> 00:23:08,211
An object contains attributes and takes tasks, as I have told.

90
00:23:08,627 --> 00:23:17,167
The attributes of an object is about the data about the entity in the real world.

91
00:23:18,003 --> 00:23:35,003
And the actions that the real world entity can take or the actions that can be used upon that real world entity will be called as methods in object-oriented language.

92
00:23:36,003 --> 00:23:43,803
Previously, I have talked about tasks, but we don't call them tasks in object orientation. We call them methods.

93
00:23:44,276 --> 00:23:56,695
